# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── Node ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
frontend/node_modules/
# frontend/dist is committed, which build output normally should not be.
#
# This gets installed at a new factory each time it is expanded, and those
# networks block the npm registry: npm resolves every version and then times
# out fetching every file, so the interface cannot be built on the machine
# that needs it. The backend serves frontend/dist itself and needs no Node at
# run time, so shipping the build means a browser download of the repository
# is a complete, working installation.
#
# It is rebuilt and committed alongside any change to frontend/src. Putting
# the rule back, as happened once, does not undo that -- it leaves index.html
# tracked and pointing at a script that is no longer committed, which serves a
# blank black page with no error anywhere.
# frontend/dist/
npm-debug.log*

# ── Runtime data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Images are excluded because they are large and reproducible from the camera.
#
# Annotations are NOT excluded, deliberately. They are small JSON files and
# they represent hours of manual work that cannot be regenerated. The previous
# .gitignore excluded them alongside the images, so a "Download ZIP" of this
# repo produced a project.json claiming 2232 annotated images with no images
# and no annotations behind it — the counts survived the trip and the work did
# not. Roughly 6000 boxes is about 2 MB of JSON; that belongs in version
# control.
data/instance/
data/instance/secret_key
data/weights/
data/projects/*/images/
data/projects/*/training/
# Annotations for generated images are excluded while hand-drawn ones are kept.
# The distinction is whether the work can be reproduced: a *_aug_* annotation is
# a copy of its source's boxes written by the augmenter and can be regenerated
# in seconds, so committing hundreds of them adds noise without protecting
# anything.
data/projects/*/annotations/*_aug_*
data/projects/*/exports/
data/projects/*/index.json

# ── Model files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.torchscript
*.blob
*.engine

# ── Logs and local env ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Bundled fonts are committed on purpose: the app must render correctly
# with no internet, so they are part of the source, not a build artefact.

# ── Editors / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
